From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doors <doors@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/canaan: vo: XRGB8888 and ARGB8888 planes get their DMA
 request bits back

Applies on top of the LILYGO BSP stack (after 0064) and Doors 0070/0071.
Doors-owned; see docs/decisions/ADR-011-kernel-patches.md and
docs/hardware/HDMI_KERNEL_FIX.md in the Doors repository.

OSD DMA_CTRL bits [3:0] are the DMA request enable and bits [5:4] the DMA
byte map: the vendor U-Boot logo code (board/canaan/common/logo/
display_logo.c, kd_vo_osd_set_dma_request() and kd_vo_osd_set_dma_map())
writes them so. The driver shipped with 0x4F for every format; BSP patch
0030 set XRGB8888 to 0x40 and ARGB8888 to 0x0, which clears the request
bits, so those planes never fetch. On the HDMI output at 1920x1080 an
XRGB8888 plane (pos-drmtest, fbdev) is black while an RGB565 plane (0x4F)
shows modetest's bars (unit A, 2026-09-27, HDMI_GATE.md round 3).

Both 32-bit formats go back to 0x4F. Bit 6, which the BSP change kept for
XRGB8888, stays set; whether the byte order it selects is right is what the
pattern's red/green/blue blocks will show.

Signed-off-by: Doors <doors@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/canaan/canaan_vo.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/canaan/canaan_vo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/canaan/canaan_vo.c
@@ -270,13 +270,23 @@
 	u32 scanout_pitch[DRM_FORMAT_MAX_PLANES];
 
 	switch (fb->format->format) {
+	/*
+	 * OSD DMA_CTRL: bits [3:0] are the DMA request enable and bits [5:4]
+	 * the DMA byte map (the vendor U-Boot logo code, display_logo.c
+	 * kd_vo_osd_set_dma_request() / kd_vo_osd_set_dma_map(), writes them
+	 * that way). The driver shipped with 0x4F for every format; the
+	 * 32-bit entries were later changed to 0x40 and 0x0, which leaves the
+	 * request bits clear, so those planes never fetch: black on the HDMI
+	 * output at 1080p while RGB565 (still 0x4F) showed a picture
+	 * (T-Display K230, unit A, 2026-09-27). Back to 0x4F for both.
+	 */
 	case DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888:
 		reg_val = 0x03;
-		rb_swap = 0x40;
+		rb_swap = 0x4F;
 		break;
 	case DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888:
 		reg_val = 0x53;
-		rb_swap = 0x0;
+		rb_swap = 0x4F;
 		break;
 	case DRM_FORMAT_ARGB4444:
 		reg_val = 0x54;
